From 25e34965a678983c29c74e17f438750673deda43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:31:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(wallpapers-ocs): set owner_id to the registered provider
 id

WallpaperOcs.items() sets owner_id to the per-network name (for example
"pling"), but the registered provider id is "ocs". import_card() calls
provider_registry.lookup(item.owner_id), so every OCS import failed with
"Wallpaper provider is not active".

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5
AI-Scope: Root-caused the owner_id mismatch and wrote the one-line fix against a live desktop session.
---
 wallpapers-ocs/wallpapers_ocs.vala | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/wallpapers-ocs/wallpapers_ocs.vala b/wallpapers-ocs/wallpapers_ocs.vala
index 278930c..c515ae0 100644
--- a/wallpapers-ocs/wallpapers_ocs.vala
+++ b/wallpapers-ocs/wallpapers_ocs.vala
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ namespace WallpapersOcs {
                 "--pages", "1", "--page-size", OCS_PAGE_SIZE}, cancel, 60, refresh);
             var result = new WallpaperProviderResult();
             result.items = WallpaperOcs.items(data, network, network_category);
+            foreach (var item in result.items) item.owner_id = id;
             var response = WallpaperOcs.document(data);
             var failed = response.get_member("failed_networks");
             if (failed != null && failed.get_node_type() == Json.NodeType.ARRAY && failed.get_array().get_length() > 0)
-- 
2.53.0

